+# agmsg
+
+Use the provided scripts. Never read or edit the SQLite store, team registry,
+Bridge boxes, or Drive queues directly.
+
+## DP Router
+
+- `DP0`: design realms, addresses, adapters, schemas, visibility, or routing.
+- `DP1`: join an identity, verify route health, send a smoke message, receive it,
+  and verify its delivery state.
+- `DP2`: use established addresses, inspect inbox/history, retry bounded failures,
+  and append audit evidence.
+
+Default basis:
+
+```text
+Basis: DP<0|1|2> / TOB-<step>
+```
+
+## Layer Contract
+
+```text
+Inko call/message/handoff semantics
+-> agmsg address, message, receipt, inbox, history
+-> local SQLite | personal Bridge | private team queue adapter
+-> filesystem / Syncthing / mounted Drive
+```
+
+`agmsg` owns all application-layer messaging. Do not let an adapter decide
+Inko call/handoff meaning, and do not let
+Inko manipulate adapter storage directly.
+
+## Address
+
+Use:
+
+```text
+<realm>:<team>/<agent>
+```
+
+Realms:
+
+- `local`: shared SQLite store; default for legacy commands.
+- `personal`: Mac/Windows Akaghef-Bridge adapter.
+- `team`: explicitly selected private Drive queue adapter.
+
+Examples:
+
+```text
+local:akaghef-system/codex
+personal:akaghef-system/mac-codex
+personal:akaghef-system/windows-codex
+team:platform/reviewer
+```
+
+`realm`, `team`, and `agent` are the logical address. Node, queue path, and
+adapter details are resolution results, not caller-visible identity.
 
